  "framing": "The Speedmaster is not just 'the Moonwatch.' That is the story that made it famous, but not where it starts. It begins as a racing chronograph in 1957, then gets pulled into one of the most important technology and exploration stories of the twentieth century — a watch with two strong identities: motorsport instrument and space-flight object. The reference trail is the fun: CK2915 the broad-arrow origin; CK2998 closer to the shape Wally Schirra wore into space; the 105.003 'Ed White' keeping the straight-lug case alive; the 105.012 and 145.012 as Moonwatch core; the 145.022 a long-running collecting universe of its own; then the branches — Alaska Project, gold Apollo XI tributes, Snoopy, X-33, Speedy Tuesday, the modern 3861.",
